      "message": "fix(2d): enter over the stock standing above a 2D op's Top instead of rapiding into it\n\nA 2D ladder whose Top sits below the material over it (Top set to the\nfirst real cut under a faced top, to skip the air pass) rapided to Top +\nthe plunge height, inside the uncut stock, and verify refused the op.\nGeneration now reads the material over the op's region (the declared\nstock less the program ahead, the #104 reading; a Contour beside a wall\nreads the band one tool diameter around it) and, only where the plain\nentry would dive under the material standing under the tool's disc,\ngenerates again with that top carried (`Approach::material_top`, never\nsaved): the first descent starts at the plunge height over it and feeds\ndown. Pocket, 2D Adaptive (spiral and trochoidal), Offset, Circular and\nContour carry it, with a `Carried stock:` note; other kinds keep the #104\nnote and the rapid law's refusal. A Top on the material, or a finish\nentering through what an earlier op cleared, posts byte-identical.\n\nFixes #1559\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
